<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to buy kerosene for May delivery.</title>
<headline>India tenders to buy kerosene for May delivery.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to buy superior kerosene oil for May delivery, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender seeks 40,000-to-45,000-tonne cargoes for delivery to Madras or Haldia on the Indian east coast, cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis.</p>
<p>The tender closes on April 3 and offers will be valid until 2200 hours, India time on April 4.  </p>
<p>In its last tender, IOC bought a 40,000-to-45,000-tonne cargo of kerosene for April delivery from Total SA at a premium of $33.40 per tonne to Mediterranean spot quotes, c-and-f Madras or Haldia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
